@startuml sm-01-job-state-machine
!include ../_style/cue.iuml
hide empty description
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor C_EXT_BD
  FontSize 12
  AttributeFontSize 11
}
skinparam state<<active>> {
  BackgroundColor C_AI_BG
  BorderColor C_AI_BD
}
skinparam state<<terminalok>> {
  BackgroundColor C_APP_BG
  BorderColor C_APP_BD
}
skinparam state<<terminalbad>> {
  BackgroundColor C_EXT_BG
  BorderColor C_EXT_BD
}
title Cue — Generation Job State Machine (animation_job.status, FR-07, NFR-03)\nEvery transition is a conditional UPDATE "WHERE status = <expected state>"

state "queued" as Q <<active>> : INSERT by API submit (idempotent)\nstarted_at, finished_at, video, frames, locked_by = NULL
state "running" as R <<active>> : set atomically by the worker claim\nstarted_at, locked_by, heartbeat_at, model_version_id NOT NULL\nfinished_at, video, frames = NULL
state "done" as D <<terminalok>> : terminal\nvideo_asset_id, frames_asset_id, frame_count,\nmodel_version_id, finished_at NOT NULL\nerror_code = NULL
state "failed" as F <<terminalbad>> : terminal\nfinished_at, error_code, error_message NOT NULL\nvideo, frames = NULL
state "cancelled" as C <<terminalbad>> : terminal\nfinished_at NOT NULL, video, frames = NULL, error_code = NULL

[*] --> Q : API: INSERT animation_job
Q --> R : Worker claim\n[row free (SKIP LOCKED) and active model_version exists]
R --> R : Worker heartbeat\n[locked_by = me]
R --> D : Worker completion\n[locked_by = me]\nINSERT frames archive + video, UPDATE in ONE transaction
R --> F : Worker error\n[locked_by = me]
R --> F : Maintenance reaper\n[heartbeat stale] error_code = worker_lost
Q --> F : Worker finds invalid input\n(input_missing, model_unavailable)
Q --> C : API cancel [owner = caller]
R --> C : API cancel [owner = caller]
D --> [*]
F --> [*]
C --> [*]

note bottom of D
  Terminal states are final: no UPDATE can leave them
  (all guards test status), so a late worker result is rejected (0 rows) and its media is discarded.
end note
legend right
  Matches database CHECK constraints animation_job_state_queued / running / done / failed / cancelled
  and animation_job_status_valid (verified by database/validation tests).
  Colours: purple = active (non-terminal), green = successful terminal, grey = failed or cancelled terminal.
  Not drawn because not committed: retry, pause, draft.
endlegend
@enduml
